---
// Damage tolerance: the flaw that NDT can miss grows to the critical size; the service life is that life divided by
// the life factor. Curve from the Paris law with m = 3: a^(-1/2) falls linearly with cycles.
const ink = 'var(--rd-ink)', muted = 'var(--rd-muted)', bad = 'var(--rd-accent)', ok = 'var(--rd-ok)', blue = 'var(--rd-blue)', steel = 'var(--rd-steel)';
const L = 44, R = 344, T = 26, B = 176;
const a0 = 0.3, ac = 1, wall = 1.18;
const X = (n: number) => L + n * (R - L), Y = (a: number) => B - (a / 1.3) * (B - T);
const aOf = (n: number) => Math.pow(Math.pow(a0, -0.5) - (Math.pow(a0, -0.5) - Math.pow(ac, -0.5)) * n, -2);
const curve = Array.from({ length: 61 }, (_, k) => k / 60).map((n) => `${X(n).toFixed(1)},${Y(aOf(n)).toFixed(1)}`).join(' ');
const q = 0.25;
---

<figure class="viz ndtlife">
  <p class="viz-title">The life is counted from the flaw that NDT can miss</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 360 215" role="img" aria-labelledby="ndtlife-desc" style="max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <desc id="ndtlife-desc">
      Crack depth against pressure cycles. The curve starts at the depth that the inspection can miss and rises, faster
      and faster, to the critical depth. The cycles between the two are the analysed life. The allowed service is that
      life divided by the life factor, here a quarter of it.
    </desc>
    <rect x={X(0)} y={T} width={X(q) - X(0)} height={B - T} fill={ok} fill-opacity="0.12"></rect>
    <line x1={L} y1={B} x2={R} y2={B} stroke={ink}></line>
    <line x1={L} y1={T} x2={L} y2={B} stroke={ink}></line>
    <line x1={L} y1={Y(wall)} x2={R} y2={Y(wall)} stroke={steel} stroke-width="2"></line>
    <text x={R} y={Y(wall) - 5} text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill={steel}>wall</text>
    <line x1={L} y1={Y(ac)} x2={R} y2={Y(ac)} stroke={bad} stroke-dasharray="6 3"></line>
    <text x={(X(q) + R) / 2} y={Y(ac) - 5} text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={bad}>critical flaw</text>
    <line x1={L} y1={Y(a0)} x2={R} y2={Y(a0)} stroke={blue} stroke-dasharray="6 3"></line>
    <text x={R} y={Y(a0) + 14} text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill={blue}>flaw that NDT can miss</text>
    <polyline points={curve} fill="none" stroke={ink} stroke-width="2.4"></polyline>
    <circle cx={X(1)} cy={Y(ac)} r="4.5" fill={bad}></circle>
    <line x1={X(1)} y1={Y(ac)} x2={X(1)} y2={B} stroke={bad} stroke-dasharray="3 3"></line>
    <text x={(X(q) + X(0)) / 2} y={T + 14} text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ok}>allowed</text>
    <text x={(X(q) + X(0)) / 2} y={T + 26} text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ok}>service</text>
    <line x1={X(0)} y1={B + 14} x2={X(1)} y2={B + 14} stroke={muted}></line>
    <line x1={X(0)} y1={B + 10} x2={X(0)} y2={B + 18} stroke={muted}></line>
    <line x1={X(1)} y1={B + 10} x2={X(1)} y2={B + 18} stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x={(X(0) + X(1)) / 2} y={B + 28} text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={muted}>analysed life = cycles from missed flaw to critical</text>
    <text x={14} y={(T + B) / 2} text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill={ink} transform={`rotate(-90 14 ${(T + B) / 2})`}>crack depth</text>
    <text x={R} y={T - 10} text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill={muted}>pressure cycles →</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The crack grows slowly at first and quickly at the end, so most of the life is spent while the crack is small. The
    allowed service is the analysed life divided by the life factor (usually four). Reusable hardware is inspected again
    before the end of that service, which starts the count again.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
